    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC successfully triggered the vulnerability. The ASAN output confirms:\n- **Heap-buffer-overflow READ of size 1** at `dns.c:1086` in `fr_dns_label_uncompressed_length`\n- Called from `decode_dns_labels` at `decode.c:354`\n- The 15-byte region `[0x6020000000f0, 0x6020000000ff)` was accessed 0 bytes to the right (i.e., exactly at byte index 15)\n\nThe PoC is a 15-byte DNS packet: 12-byte header (qdcount=1) + 3 bytes of question data (`\\x03ab`). The label declares 3 characters but only 2 are present in the buffer. The buggy `buf_len` calculation inflates the end pointer by 12 bytes (the offset of question data within the packet), allowing the label validator to read 1 byte past the heap allocation.",
